Draw surfaces at their buffer scale; report the desktop's device scale

On a scaled desktop (air/OS: BScreen::DeviceScale(), looked up at run
time) wl_output reports the device scale rounded up, with the mode in
pixels of that scale, so clients such as GTK and Firefox draw their
buffers at that density instead of at the logical size, which app_server
then had to enlarge. A surface with a buffer scale covers its buffer
size divided by the scale: drawn one to one where the desktop has the
same density (200 percent), filtered down where it is lower (150, 175
percent). Buffer damage and viewport sources follow the scale, and a
cursor drawn at a higher density is averaged down to logical pixels.

